            <ArticleTitle>Traditional Kehr's sign: Left shoulder pain related to splenic abscess.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>87-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5505/tjtes.2011.04874</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Kehrs sign was originally described by the German surgeon Hans Kehr (1862-1916). It is a classical example of referred pain: irritation of the diaphragm is signaled by the phrenic nerve as pain in the area above the clavicle. We present a case of a 21-year-old woman admitted to the emergency department with the chief complaint of left shoulder pain related to splenic abscess.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
